Passerine Tick:
1.Biocharacteristics:
1 year lifespan,Targets Birds,Human bites are rare, reddish-brown to blackish(solid coloured no patterns),size 2.3mm -  8.0mm,body is oval,hairy and fuzzy.

2.Habitat:
lives in leaf litter under bamboo bushes,high humid areas.

3.Health Risks:

Health Risks to Humans:
Lyme Borreliosis,Tick-Borne Encephalitis,Anaplasma phagocytophilum (agent of human granulocytic anaplasmosis) and Borrelia miyamotoi (relapsing fever).

Health Risks to Animals:
Passerines act as hosts for tick larvae and nymphs, supporting their life cycle, which indirectly impacts other wildlife by increasing the tick population.
Domestic Animals: The ticks carried by birds (such as I. ricinus) can drop off into domestic environments, posing risks to pets and livestock.
Impact on Birds: While some studies show minimal impact on overall bird condition, high infestations of Ixodes ricinus can cause negative health effects on small passerine hosts.
